me never came close to recovering it.", "moments": [{"turn": 7, "text": "The 12k's G2 was its worst move of the game, losing 5.3 points. It swung Black's lead from +1.4 to -3.9, with the engine preferring F4. After that, Opus 5.5 had the better side of the board."}, {"turn": 10, "text": "Opus 5.5 was ahead, with Black's lead at -5.0, but D3 lost 5.7 points and put Black back in front at +0.7. The engine wanted G3. This is where the early edge was lost."}, {"turn": 12, "text": "F5 lost another 4.4 points and moved Black's lead from +0.7 to +5.1. The engine preferred F6. By this point Black's stones at G4 and G5 formed a wall along the G-file beside White's group."}, {"turn": 14, "text": "D6 was the blunder of the game, 7.2 points lost. It pushed Black's lead from +5.0 to +12.3, and the engine's choice was E7, which Black then took on the next move. The lead never dropped below +12.3 again."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "B8 matched the engine's first choice, and Opus 5.5 lost nothing on it. It was the one clean move in a corner fight on the left where White stones on B7, B8, C7 and the C3 to B3 line were holding their ground, though the lead stayed above +14."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "Opus 5.5 kept pressing on the right with J5, but it lost 4.4 points and Black's lead went from +14.6 to +19.0. The engine's choice was C9. Several of Opus 5.5's moves in this stretch lost 3.6 to 4.4 points each, and the 12k answered, so the lead stayed in the mid-teens until the resignation."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and report group liberties and an area count of the current position, and the other commands just cat/tail/append to games.md notes; nothing chooses moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}